1
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:05,310
A migration isn't finished
when the records arrive.

2
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:08,830
It's finished when the business
can do real work in the new books.

3
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:12,490
MoveBooks calls that first productive use.

4
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:13,590
In start,

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,030
finish the essentials,

6
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,750
then review a draft
invoice to Cedar School.

7
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:18,770
One line,

8
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:20,190
catalog preparation,

9
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:21,630
for $100.

10
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:25,490
The sales tax code CA-SALES at

11
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:29,690
7.25% adds $7.25 for

12
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:32,450
a total of $107.25.

13
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:34,810
nothing posts on its own.

14
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:39,710
You approve the invoice terms and the
screen records who approved them and

15
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:40,210
when.

16
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:44,330
Only then can you post it. Posting
creates a balanced journal entry.

17
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:47,530
Accounts receivable is debited 107.25,

18
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:52,350
sales is credited 100 and
tax payable is credited 7.25.

19
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:55,090
The rules confirm that
debits equal credits.

20
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:59,870
If a connection drops and you post
again, the retry reuses the original

21
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:04,150
key so The completed work is never
repeated, and the invoice can't be posted

22
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:04,650
twice.

23
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:06,930
Then the rules verify it.

24
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:08,230
Posted and verified,

25
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:12,830
107.25 equals 100 plus 7.25 in tax.

26
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:15,170
Readiness shows 10 of 10 checks.

27
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:19,950
Invoice checks, 6 of 6, and the trial
balance still shows no difference.

28
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:22,010
Harbor Light Books is ready to use.

